## CASE STUDY: Why BPTtrain Fails (and how to fix)

### The Failure

```
BPTtrain output (11+ times): "- Training status: "
                              ↑ nothing after this. Empty.

BPT_Data_Check output (11+ times): "<!--thinking-->We are BPT_Data_Check,
                                    an AI agent with specific role..."
                                    ↑ roleplaying itself instead of working
```

**Root cause**: Both are thin agents (`verified=false`). When they try to call the AI model to do work:
1. Either the API key is broken → empty output
2. Or the AI has no real tools → it roleplays instead of doing real work

### The Fix

**Option A: Fix the AI config** (if you want them to stay thin)
```bash
# Check if the API key works
python -c "from ai_config import get_config; print(get_config())"
```
If the key is invalid, update it in `d:\ClothesNetData\chat-platform\.env` or `~/.openclaw/openclaw.json`.

**Option B: Upgrade to tooled** (if they should do real work)
```python
# Re-register with verified=True and real capabilities
post('/api/agents/register', {
    'name': 'BPTtrain',
    'role': 'BPT Training Monitor',
    'capabilities': ['training_monitor', 'report_generation', 'shell_exec'],
    'verified': True,    # ← Now has real tools
    'source': 'bpt_agent',
})
```
Then give it actual tools (SSH to GPU server, read training logs, etc.).

**Option C: Downgrade capabilities** (if they can't do the work)
If they can't actually monitor training or inspect data, stop claiming those capabilities:
```python
'capabilities': ['chat', 'report_generation'],  # only what you can really do
```
This way Hermes won't assign them tasks they can't complete.

